# The Gates Learjet 35A's checklists: this project's own, in its own words.
#
# **They are not taken from the aeroplane's flight manual.** No such
# manual was read to write them. What they follow is the ordinary
# practice for the type, in the order it is flown; the speeds and
# settings in them are this project's own figures, assets/figures/learjet35a.xml,
# whose sources docs/ASSETS.md records, and the flight model itself
# wherever the model is what decides - a lever's gate, a flap's travel,
# an engine's idle.
#
#   phase NAME                       one of: before-start, taxi, take-off,
#                                    climb, cruise, descent, approach,
#                                    landing, after-landing
#   check PROPERTY OP VALUE TEXT...  an item the aircraft can see done
#   range PROPERTY LOW HIGH TEXT...  the same, where a band shows it done
#   confirm TEXT...                  an item only the pilot can see done
#
# with `#` beginning a comment; src/sim/checklist.hpp owns the format.
#
# The 35A's TFE731s are turbofans: there is no mixture and no pitch lever, so
# nothing here names either, and the thrust set is read off the fan, N1 - 30
# per cent at idle, 100 at take-off. Its spoilers are its airbrake and its
# lift dump both, and it has no thrust reverser in this model, so the landing
# run is the wheel brakes' work.
#
# The speeds are worked from the flight manual's charts as
# assets/figures/learjet35a.xml quotes them: the stall with flaps 40 at the
# maximum landing weight, 96.5 knots, sets a threshold speed a third above it;
# the stall with flaps 8, 109 knots at 15,800 lb, sets the band the nose comes
# up in across the weights. Mmo is 0.81 and the ceiling 45,000 feet, both the
# manual's own.

phase before-start
confirm Walk-round done, covers and pins off, and the cabin door shut and latched
check fcs/throttle-cmd-norm <= 0.05 Thrust levers closed
check fcs/flap-pos-deg <= 0.5 Flaps up
check fcs/speedbrake-pos-norm <= 0.05 Spoilers in
range fcs/pitch-trim-cmd-norm -0.35 0.35 Pitch trim set within the take-off band
confirm Fuel quantity and balance checked, the tip tanks counted in

phase taxi
check propulsion/engine[0]/n2 >= 55 Left engine running, N2 up to its idle of 60 per cent
check propulsion/engine[1]/n2 >= 55 Right engine running
range fcs/flap-pos-deg 7.5 8.5 Flaps eight degrees, the take-off setting
confirm Brakes and nosewheel steering checked as the aeroplane first moves
check fcs/throttle-cmd-norm <= 0.35 Taxi at idle thrust, held back on the brakes rather than the levers

phase take-off
range fcs/flap-pos-deg 7.5 8.5 Flaps eight degrees
check fcs/speedbrake-pos-norm <= 0.05 Spoilers in
check gear/gear-pos-norm >= 0.95 Undercarriage down and locked for the roll
check propulsion/engine[0]/n1 >= 90 Take-off thrust set, the fans up near 100 per cent
range velocities/vc-kts 100 140 The nose up at 128 knots at the maximum weight, less as it lightens
confirm Airspeed alive on both sides, the engine instruments in the green, the runway clear

phase climb
check gear/gear-pos-norm <= 0.05 Undercarriage up
check fcs/flap-pos-deg <= 0.5 Flaps up once the second segment is behind
range propulsion/engine[0]/n1 80 100 Climb thrust set
range velocities/vc-kts 200 280 Climb at 250 knots, and on Mach above the changeover
confirm Pressurisation climbing with the aeroplane, and the seat-belt sign on

phase cruise
range velocities/mach 0.60 0.81 Cruise held below Mach 0.81, the Mmo
range position/h-sl-ft 25000 45000 Level in the flight levels, at or under the ceiling of 45,000 feet
check fcs/flap-pos-deg <= 0.5 Flaps up
check gear/gear-pos-norm <= 0.05 Undercarriage up
check fcs/speedbrake-pos-norm <= 0.05 Spoilers in

phase descent
range propulsion/engine[0]/n1 25 75 Thrust back for the descent
range velocities/vc-kts 150 300 Down at 250 to 300 knots, the spoilers used if the profile needs them
confirm Altimeters set to the field's pressure at the transition level
confirm Pressurisation set to the field's height, and the approach briefed

phase approach
check gear/gear-pos-norm >= 0.95 Undercarriage down and locked, three greens
range fcs/flap-pos-deg 19.0 41.0 Flaps twenty on the base leg, forty on the final
range velocities/vc-kts 120 160 Approach at 130 knots, a third above the stall with full flap
check fcs/speedbrake-pos-norm <= 0.05 Spoilers in from the final approach fix
confirm Landing clearance given, the runway in sight and the lights on

phase landing
check fcs/flap-pos-deg >= 39.0 Flaps forty degrees
check gear/gear-pos-norm >= 0.95 Undercarriage down and locked
range velocities/vc-kts 115 135 Over the threshold at 125 knots at the maximum landing weight
check fcs/throttle-cmd-norm <= 0.15 Thrust levers closed in the flare
check fcs/speedbrake-pos-norm >= 0.5 Spoilers out on touchdown, to put the weight on the wheels

phase after-landing
check fcs/flap-pos-deg <= 0.5 Flaps up
check fcs/speedbrake-pos-norm <= 0.05 Spoilers in
check velocities/vc-kts <= 30 Clear of the runway and slowed to a taxi
check fcs/throttle-cmd-norm <= 0.2 Thrust levers at idle
confirm Landing and strobe lights off, and the transponder to standby
